<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Offline RL</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the offline reinforcement learning experiments on Atari, we use datasets from RL Unplugged<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/huihanl/rl_unplugged" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/huihanl/rl_unplugged</a></span></span></span> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gulcehre et al. (2020)</a></cite>), which provide standardized and diverse benchmarks. The implementation is built on a stable and well-tested codebase to ensure reproducibility and fair comparison. The code will be shared upon acceptance. All methods are run with their default hyperparameters, and the most important settings are reported in Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ C.3 Offline RL ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ Use the Online Network If You Can: Towards Fast and Stable Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
